8 est

@Hunter Welborn  arrives at the DHR garage thrilled for the biggest opportunity of his career. The DHR crew welcomes him with open arms and surprises him with a custom DHR driver’s suit made just for his tryout. But earning a spot won’t be easy. DHR has a full slate of tryout tasks Hunter must complete throughout the day before they decide if he’s worthy of joining the team.

Meanwhile, @Jim Segredo storms over to Bryce’s hauler, furious, and calls for @Alex Leebaw to come with him. Unfortunately, Alex has already gotten into the Sugar Shocker cereal and Orange Tang, turning an already hectic morning into complete chaos.

2 est 

@Hunter Welborn ‘s next tryout challenge sends him straight into the garage. The DHR crew points to a spotless race car and tells him there’s “something seriously wrong with the left rear.” They give him 1 hour to diagnose the issue. Hunter inspects every inch of the car, only to discover he’d been searching for a problem that never existed.

Meanwhile, the High Line leadership team sits down with Hendrick Motorsports to finalize a technical alliance for superspeedway events. As part of the agreement, @#100 Eric Hayden agrees to transfer two of Pedley’s mechanics to work race weekends for HMS

3 est 

@Hunter Welborn ‘s next tryout challenge is all about proving he can work under pressure. While the entire DHR team relaxes in lawn chairs watching the show, Hunter is left alone to change a tire as quickly as he can. As he struggles to beat the clock, @Shame Hatfield strolls by, grins, and can’t resist saying: 

Meanwhile, the High Line crew wraps up its visit to the Hendrick Motorsports campus and begins heading home. Everyone had a productive day, but @Alex Leebaw is still buzzing with excitement after meeting his favorite driver.
